%% ======================================================================================
%% K0-K1 BRIDGE - DETAILED ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM
%% ======================================================================================
%% Created: 2026-02-01
%% Updated: 2026-02-01 - IFL moved to Bridge (Option B: Bridge owns IFL)
%% Updated: 2026-02-01 - Added offline-first architecture (K1 self-sufficient)
%% Updated: 2026-02-01 - Added complete envelope, query, SSE schemas from K0 ports
%% Updated: 2026-02-01 - Added observability/feedback flow from FEEDBACK.md + observe.py
%% Updated: 2026-02-01 - Fixed flow directions per K0/K1 skeleton diagrams
%% Purpose: Bridge as central security gateway between K0 and K1
%% Location: bridge/ (root level - NOT inside K0 or K1)
%% EDGE-FIRST DESIGN PRINCIPLE:
%%   - K1 is self-sufficient (works offline with reduced functionality)
%%   - K0 is enhancement layer (cross-device sync, long-term memory, KG)
%%   - Bridge handles K0 availability gracefully (queue when offline)
%%   - SessionState COLD tier is LOCAL to K1 (not K0 dependent)
%% FLOW DIRECTIONS (Corrected):
%%   - Command: K1 -> K0 (ONE-WAY fire-and-forget, no response)
%%   - Query:   K1 -> K0 -> K1 (REQUEST/RESPONSE, two-way)
%%   - SSE:     K0 -> K1 (ONE-WAY streaming, K0 pushes events)
%%   - Feedback: K1 -> K0 (ONE-WAY via obs.emit kind=feedback)
%%   - IFL:     BIDIRECTIONAL to devices (K1 operates, inbound data -> K0)
%% K0 PORTS (Bridge connects to):
%%   - /k0/command.submit  - POST - Write any topic (ONE-WAY, no response)
%%   - /k0/query.recall    - POST - Multi-selector recall bundles (REQUEST/RESPONSE)
%%   - /k0/sse.subscribe   - GET  - Real-time event stream (K0 -> K1 STREAMING)
%%   - /k0/obs.emit        - POST - Telemetry + Feedback (ONE-WAY)
%% COMMAND TOPICS (What K1 writes to K0):
%%   memory.delta        → P02 (Episodic memory from conversations)
%%   session.checkpoint  → P02 (SessionState snapshots)
%%   beliefs.archive     → P02 (Evicted beliefs from SessionState)
%%   history.archive     → P02 (Evicted turn history from SessionState)
%%   plan.committed      → P02 (Planner Stage 4 committed plans)
%%   device.event.*      → P02 (IFL inbound sensor data)
%%   learning.feedback   → P06 (K1 feedback signals)
%%   sync.delta          → P07 (CRDT device sync)
%% QUERY SELECTORS (RecallSelector types):
%%   type: episodic  - topic: memory.delta   - WAL position recall
%%   type: semantic  - query: free-text      - pgvector similarity
%%   type: session   - topic: session.*      - SessionState history
%%   type: device    - topic: device.event.* - IFL event history
%% SSE EVENTS (K0 → K1):
%%   SSETraceEvent: cursor, topic, wal_pos, commit_ts, policy_stamp
%%   memory.formed.v1         - Memory consolidation complete
%%   k0.learning.advisory.v1  - Validated feedback signal
%%   k0.proactive.signal.v1   - Proactive agent trigger
%%   k0.sync.complete.v1      - Device sync finished
%%   cognitive.vector.stored.v1 - Embedding indexed
%%   Backpressure: level (ok/throttle/shed), lag_ms, pending_events
%% OBSERVABILITY KINDS (/k0/obs.emit):
%%   kind: metrics  - snapshot (prometheus format), captured_at, source
%%   kind: logs     - entries[]: message, level, event, cognitive_trace_id
%%   kind: feedback - FeedbackEnvelope (see below)
%% TWO-SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE (Learning/Feedback):
%%   SYSTEM 1: GAP RESOLUTION (Active Learning Loop)
%%     Purpose: Add NEW FACTS to memory by asking users
%%     Flow: P03 gap → st_learning_queue → P06 → P05 Attention → curiosity.intent.v1 (SSE)
%%           → K1 Curiosity Agent → User answers → Command Port (memory.delta + gap_id)
%%           → P02 → st_hipp_events → P03 resolves gap
%%     Port: Command Port (user answer IS new content)
%%   SYSTEM 2: MODEL REFINEMENT (Algorithm Tuning)
%%     Purpose: Tune weights/thresholds based on behavioral signals
%%     Flow: K1 detects signal → FeedbackEnvelope → Obs Port (kind=feedback)
%%           → P21 validates → st_feedback_signals → feedback.signal.<pipeline>.v1
%%           → P02/P03/P08 learning modules → st_learned_weights
%%     Port: Obs Port (tunes algorithms, not creates facts)
%% FEEDBACK ENVELOPE (K1 → K0 via obs.emit kind=feedback):
%%   feedback_id, pipeline_id (P02/P06/P08), tenant_id, space_id
%%   signal_class: CORRECTION | VALIDATION | IMPLICIT | EXPLICIT | OUTCOME
%%   signal_subtype: user_correction, reformulation_detected, etc.
%%   correlation: session_id, event_ids[], wal_positions[], recall_id, target_entity_id
%%   provenance: source_message_id, recall_context_hash, feedback_timestamp
%%   payload: pipeline-specific (P02FeedbackPayload, P08FeedbackPayload)
%%   K0 persists to st_feedback_signals → BusDispatcher → feedback.signal.<pipeline>.v1
%% ENVELOPE V1 (CommandEnvelope schema):
%%   cognitive_trace_id, tenant_id, space_id
%%   topic, schema_uri, body
%%   actor, device_id, band
%%   sig_alg (Ed25519), sig_kid, sig
%%   envelope_sha256 (full envelope integrity)
%%   idem_key (BLAKE3 derived, duplicate detection)
%% This diagram shows:
%%   - K1 TOUCHPOINTS (Left): Where K1 components connect TO Bridge
%%   - K1 LOCAL STORAGE (Left): K1's own SQLite for offline operation
%%   - BRIDGE INTERNALS (Center): All responsibilities + offline awareness
%%   - K0 TOUCHPOINTS (Right): Where Bridge connects TO K0 (optional cloud)
%%   - PHYSICAL DEVICES (Right): Where Bridge IFL connects to external devices
%%   - FAMILY DEVICES (Bottom): Multi-device sync mesh
%% Five Responsibilities:
%%   1. Kernel Transport: K0 ↔ K1 memory/storage communication
%%   2. Connector Security: Tool registration, auth, rate limiting
%%   3. Device Sync: Multi-device family sync via K0 P07
%%   4. IFL (Interkernel Fabric Language): Device protocol adapters (BRIDGE OWNED)
%%   5. Offline Awareness: Queue commands when K0 unavailable, drain when back
%% ======================================================================================

